{"name":"Foxtail","hex":"#bc896e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foxtail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tail of a fox.","A dry spikelet or spikelet seed and flower cluster of some grasses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foxtail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Foxtail (diaspore)","blocks":[{"text":"A foxtail is a spikelet or cluster of a grass, that serves to disperse its seeds as a unit. Thus, the foxtail is a type of diaspore or plant dispersal unit. Some grasses that produce a foxtail are themselves called \"foxtail\", also \"spear grass\". They can become a health hazard for dogs, cats, and other domestic animals, and a nuisance for people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Hordeum_murinum_in_Voorhis_Ecological_Reserve%2CCal_Poly_Pomona.jpg/330px-Hordeum_murinum_in_Voorhis_Ecological_Reserve%2CCal_Poly_Pomona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foxtail_(diaspore)"},{"title":"Alopecurus","blocks":[{"text":"Alopecurus, or foxtail grass, is a common and widespread genus of plants in the grass family. It is common across temperate and subtropical parts of Eurasia, northern Africa, and the Americas, as well as naturalized in Australia and on various islands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Alopecurus_myosuroides1.jpg/330px-Alopecurus_myosuroides1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alopecurus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Hordeum_murinum_disarticulating_spikelet_cluster.jpg/120px-Hordeum_murinum_disarticulating_spikelet_cluster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Hordeum_murinum_disarticulating_spikelet_cluster.jpg/250px-Hordeum_murinum_disarticulat